// Three tiny real ALAC files, checked in as text because the compressed
// paths of a codec cannot be exercised by bytes a test builds by hand — a
// hand-written encoder would only ever mirror the decoder's own idea of the
// format. These were produced by an independent implementation instead:
// ffmpeg 6.1.1's ALAC encoder, fed PCM from the deterministic generator in
// test-alac-decoder.mjs. ALAC is lossless, so the test regenerates that PCM
// and requires the decoded output to match it exactly — an assertion that
// depends on neither our decoder nor ffmpeg's.
//
// To rebuild (sizes in test-alac-decoder.mjs describe the layout):
//   1. write the generator's output as raw PCM (s16le / s24le, 8000 Hz)
//   2. ffmpeg -f s16le -ar 8000 -ac <n> -i raw.pcm -c:a alac out.m4a
//   3. base64 the result into this file
//
// 8704 frames each: two full 4096-sample ALAC packets plus one partial.

